{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/572378-what-sort-of-occult-rituals-did-they-have-in-demon-the-fallen","id":572378,"title":"What sort of Occult Rituals did they have in Demon: the Fallen?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-29T00:45:21-07:00","id":572378,"title":"What sort of Occult Rituals did they have in Demon: the Fallen?","content":"I know that there are your basic Summon/Bind/Incarnate rituals. Those are standard. Then you have the rituals that allow you to prepare a Reliquary for a Fallen that costs permanent Willpower. Then you have the Exorcist list of rituals. And you have the Earthbound worship rituals. I am asking this question because I am thinking that a Fallen with Occult 5 and an Apocalyptic Feature that gives a -2 to the difficulty of the roll might be able to devise a ritual where he can use a Thrall who's soul he owns and is linked to him in a Pact to pay the Permanent Will cost for him in order for him to attune himself to a Relic so he doesn't have to spend Permanent Faith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T09:45:38-07:00","id":574047,"title":"","content":"I'm a bit confused. Most relics do not require Permanent Faith. Is the relic you are talking about one of the few (or a house-ruled addition) that does require such a sacrifice or attunement? If so, then it seems like that Relic may be important and powerful enough that no substitution would be acceptable (from a story perspective), nor would substitution be balanced (from a game perspective).<br /> <br /> Either way, I'm afraid I do not think your proposed ritual is quite right. Please let me elaborate.<br /> <br /> Yes, it might be possible (though very difficult and time-consuming) for one of the Fallen to design a ritual of sacrifice substitution. And yes, it might be possible to convince enough mortals to perform the ritual (remember that mortals are necessary for most non-Lore rituals). But if the Relic requires Permanent Faith, then a mortal's Permanent Willpower is not going to be sufficient; Faith and Willpower are very different energies. If anything, such a ritual would permanently lower the Thrall's Faith potential instead (and should probably add a lot of Torment to the Demon in question), as that would be a more comparable sacrifice.<br /> <br /> If this is your game, and you see a need for such a ritual to exist, then I suggest making it 1) Rare; 2) Very time-consuming to research and perform; 3) Very difficult to perform correctly; 4) Require the willing sacrifice of a Thrall's Faith potential; 5) Count as a major sin, at least an &quot;8&quot; on the Hierarchy of Sins table","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />Avatar commissioned from the incomparable Melissa Uran.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/966-redford_blade","name":"Redford_Blade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar966_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-30T22:45:34-07:00","id":574804,"title":"","content":"Some Relics work better if you attune to them. For a mortal, this requires a Perm Willpower. For Demons, this requires Perm Faith.<br /> <br /> I suspect it works this way because of how incredible the human soul is supposed to be. You can ravage a soul for willpower to turn into Faith points, but demons don't seem to have spirits that allow their Will to become Faith.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","user":"Mercurial","date":". 07-01-2015, 01:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T17:23:16-07:00","id":671513,"title":"","content":"Maybe i'm just weird, but sometimes i get a very strong feeling the Fallen are just a bunch of crazed denizens of the Dreaming shaped by different myths brought into the human world like the Kithain, Thallain or Adhene by major spiritual shake-ups.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-19T18:32:39-07:00","id":671580,"title":"","content":"personally, that to me has no flavor, I don't see why you couldn't do it but it is just playing with numbers instead of adding interesting benefits or disadvantages","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T20:34:22-07:00","id":672829,"title":"","content":"Don't forget that mortals can also participate in the Lore-Based Rituals of the Fallen (See Players Guide).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-22T15:24:24-08:00","id":771760,"title":"","content":"Well, we have in Demon quite a number of rituals with a lot of distinctions.<br /> <br /> Summon, Binding and Exorcism aren't demonic rituals in a technical sense. Those rituals can be developed by mortals with or without demonic help, but only mortals can perform them, with their Faith Potential.<br /> <br /> &quot;Incarnation&quot; of a Demon isn't a ritual, though some powerful demons need specially prepared Reliquaries to contain their souls without breaking. But the actual act of possessing and so incarnate upon something isn't a ritual, just a thing a demon can do (a poor vessel just breaks over time from the exposure to such energy, but a demon can hop from pen to pencil to eraser if she wants).<br /> <br /> A Demon can Ravage Willpower from her thralls for a lot of things, but it isn't a ritual either. Curiously she can Ravage them even for actual demonic rituals, but those have to do with Lore, not Thralldom. No ritual FOR Ravaging was ever mentioned at all.<br /> <br /> You could make a case for Ravaging to Attune to a Relic. I don't think it would be a demonic ritual, though. Probably a human Faith ritual or a condition of the Pact would suits this effect better. So, in the bargain you make the mortal promise you energy to do such a thing, and then you can do it because the Pact provides the means.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}